      "evidence": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "5d3ced87-e0eb-4329-86e0-ceb39f0ce641",
          "source_type": "news_article",
          "source_title": "Broadcom's Real Risk Is Its Customer List",
          "source_url": "https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/broadcoms-real-risk-customer-list-123150324.html?fr=sycsrp_catchall",
          "publisher": "finance.yahoo.com",
          "extracted_fact": "Six Core Customers Carry The Accelerator Business The custom accelerators inside Broadcom's AI semiconductor line are built for six core customers. One of the six holds a long-term agreement covering multiple generations of TPUs, Broadcom has a contractual commitment to deploy 1.3 gigawatts for OpenAI in 2027, and Meta's MTIA X deployment is planned through the end of 2028. Six Core Customers Carry The Accelerator Business",
          "excerpt": "Six Core Customers Carry The Accelerator Business\n\nThe custom accelerators inside Broadcom's AI semiconductor line are built for six core customers. One of the six holds a long-term agreement covering multiple generations of TPUs, Broadcom has a contractual commitment to deploy 1.3 gigawatts for OpenAI in 2027, and Meta's MTIA X deployment is planned through the end of 2028. The order book behind that list is genuinely deep: AI bookings topped $30 billion in fiscal Q2 2026 against $10.8 billion actually shipped, and management put its forward visibility at 2028. [...] In fiscal Q2 2026, AI semiconductors accounted for 49% of quarterly revenue of $22.2 billion, by the company's own breakdown. That is no longer a growth business bolted onto a diversified chip and software franchise; it is the franchise. The fiscal Q3 2026 guide is heavier still: $16 billion of AI semiconductor revenue inside $29.4 billion of consolidated revenue, roughly 54% of the total. That consolidated figure is itself a sharp step up from the $22.2 billion just reported. Broadcom is not diversifying into AI so much as converting into it.\n\nSix Core Customers Carry The Accelerator Business\nOops, something went wrong\n\n[Skip to navigation](#navigation-container)  [Skip to right column](#right-rail) \n\n\n[Sign in](https://login.yahoo.com/?done=https%3A%2F%2Ffinance.yahoo.com%2Ftechnology%2Fai%2Farticles%2Fbroadcoms-real-risk-customer-list-123150324.html%3Ffr%3Dsycsrp_catchall&intl=us&lang=en-US&activity=ybar-sign",
          "page_text": "Six Core Customers Carry The Accelerator Business\n\nThe custom accelerators inside Broadcom's AI semiconductor line are built for six core customers. One of the six holds a long-term agreement covering multiple generations of TPUs, Broadcom has a contractual commitment to deploy 1.3 gigawatts for OpenAI in 2027, and Meta's MTIA X deployment is planned through the end of 2028. The order book behind that list is genuinely deep: AI bookings topped $30 billion in fiscal Q2 2026 against $10.8 billion actually shipped, and management put its forward visibility at 2028. [...] In fiscal Q2 2026, AI semiconductors accounted for 49% of quarterly revenue of $22.2 billion, by the company's own breakdown. That is no longer a growth business bolted onto a diversified chip and software franchise; it is the franchise. The fiscal Q3 2026 guide is heavier still: $16 billion of AI semiconductor revenue inside $29.4 billion of consolidated revenue, roughly 54% of the total. That consolidated figure is itself a sharp step up from the $22.2 billion just reported. Broadcom is not diversifying into AI so much as converting into it.\n\nSix Core Customers Carry The Accelerator Business\nOops, something went wrong\n\n[Skip to navigation](#navigation-container)  [Skip to right column](#right-rail) \n\n\n[Sign in](https://login.yahoo.com/?done=https%3A%2F%2Ffinance.yahoo.com%2Ftechnology%2Fai%2Farticles%2Fbroadcoms-real-risk-customer-list-123150324.html%3Ffr%3Dsycsrp_catchall&intl=us&lang=en-US&activity=ybar-signin&pspid=1183300100&src=finance)\n\n1. [My Portfolio](https://finance.yahoo.com/portfolios/)\n2. 1. [Stocks](https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/) \n      1. [Most Active](https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/most-active/)\n      2. [Day Gainers](https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/gainers/)\n      3. [Day Losers](https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/losers/)\n      4. [Trending](https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/trending/)\n      5. [Hi