          "page_text": "FAQ :: Intel Corporation (INTC)\nIntel.com\nInvestors\nOverview\nAbout Intel\nContacts\nCompany Overview\nManagement Team\nNews & Events\nOverview\nPress Releases\nIR Calendar\nAnnual Stockholders’ Meeting\nInvestor Meeting\nEmail Alerts\nPresentations\nFinancial Info\nOverview\nFinancial Results\nBalance Sheet\nIncome Statement\nCash Flow\nStock Info\nQuote\nCharts\nHistorical Data\nStock Splits\nDividends & Buybacks\nMobileye Acquisition\nFAQ\nFilings & Reports\nOverview\nAll SEC Filings\nAnnual Reports\nQuarterly Reports\nSection 16 Filings\nIRS Forms\nOrder Publications\nBoard & Governance\nOverview\nBoard of Directors\nBoard Committees\nGovernance Documents\nEngagement & Outreach\nContact the Board\nESG\nFAQ\nStock Info\nStock Info\nQuote\nCharts\nHistorical Data\nStock Splits\nDividends & Buybacks\nMobileye Acquisition\nFAQ\nWhat are Intel's ticker and CUSIP?\nIntel's stock symbol is INTC\nIntel common stock is traded on the NASDAQ Global Select Market\nOur fiscal year end is the last Saturday in December.\nIntel Common stock CUSIP is 458140-10-0\nWhen was Intel's initial public offering and the IPO price?\nIntel went public October 13, 1971 at a price of USD 23.50 per share or 2 cents adjusted for our 13 subsequent stock splits.\nWhat year and place was Intel Corporation incorporated?\nIntel was incorporated 3/1/89 in Delaware. Below is the history from Intel California to the current Intel Delaware:\n7/18/68 Incorporated: California, as NM Electronics Inc.\n8/6/68 Name changed to Intel Corporation, a California Corporation.\n3/1/89 Incorporation of Intel Corporation, a Delaware Corporation.\n5/5/89 Intel Corporation (California) merged with and into Intel Corporation (Delaware). Intel Corporation (Delaware) is the surviving corporation.\nWho is Intel's accounting firm?\nErnst & Young LLP. They have been Intel's auditors since the company's inception in 1968.\nWho is Intel's transfer agent?\nIntel's Transfer agent is Computershare Investor Services LLC. Contact them for financial literature or stockholder services, to transfer stock, or to change your address. Current stockholders can get full portfolio access to their Intel Corporation account(s) by registering on the\nComputershare Web site\nBy Phone:\nIn the U.S. tollfree: 1-800-298-0146\nOutside the U.S. direct dial: 1-312-360-5123\nOr by fax: 1-312-601-4332\nBy email:\nweb.queries@computershare.com\nBy Regular Mail\nComputershare\nPO Box 43078\nProvidence, RI 02940-3078\nUnited States\nBy Overnight Delivery\nComputershare\n150 Royall Street\nSuite 101\nCanton, MA 02021\nUnited States\nIs there an option to purchase and/or reinvest dividends in Intel shares directly?\nYes. Through\nComputershare\n.\nWhere can I obtain Intel's quarterly reports?\nIntel files quarterly reports (-Form 10-Q) with the SEC, which can be accessed\nhere\n. We post the\nearnings releases\nand\nquarterly financial statements\n. The earnings release and Form 10Q are also available from\nComputershare Investor Services LLC\nat 1-800-298-0146 or 1-312-360-5123 from other U.S. locations; outside the U.S. at 1-312-360-5123.\nHow can I reach the Investor Relations Department?\nFor other investor inquiries or to contact someone in our Investor Relations department, please contact us at:\nIntel Corporation\nRNB 4-148\n2200 Mission College Blvd\nSanta Clara, California 95054\nUSA\nPhone: 1-408-765-1480\nInvestor.Relations@intel.com\nWhen was Intel's stockholder meeting?\nInformation about Intel’s most recent Annual Stockholders’ Meeting can be found\nhere\n.\nEmail Alerts\nTear Sheet\nContacts\nRSS News Feed\nMarket Data copyright © 2026\nQuoteMedia\n. Data delayed 15 minutes unless otherwise indicated (view\ndelay times\nfor all exchanges).\nRT\n=Real-Time,\nEOD\n=End of Day,\nPD\n=Previous Day. Market Data powered by\nQuoteMedia\n.\nTerms of Use\n.",
