          "excerpt": "Release Calendar\nTechDocs\nLogin\n|\nRegister\nContinuous Delivery Director SaaS\nCHANGE VERSION\n1.0\nEnglish\nOverview\nRelease Notes\nAbout Continuous Delivery Director\nGetting Started (SaaS)\nRelease Orchestration\nRelease Design\nRelease Management\nRelease Execution\nRelease Tracks\nCalendars\nRelease Calendar\nMaintenance Windows\nEnvironment Planner\nFreeze Periods\nReports\nTest Orchestration\nSecurity\nIntegrations\nDocumentation Legal Notice\nAdministration\nProduct Tutorial Videos\nReference\nDocumentation Legal Notice\nHome\nContinuous Delivery Director SaaS\n...\nRelease Orchestration\nCalendars\nRelease Calendar\nRelease Calendar\nThe Release Calendar provides a high-level, interactive calendar view of all planned and running releases.\nDownload PDF\nRelease Calendar\nThe Release Calendar provides a high-level, interactive calendar view of all planned and running releases.\nThe calendar acts as a real-time release dashboard with configurations saved per user. Use the calendar to plan resource use across teams and releases. You can see the Releases in separate lines on the left of the calendar.\nYou access the\nRelease Calendar\nfrom the\nCalendars\ntab.\nAs a release owner or member, you can use the visual release calendar to monitor the following information:\nReal-time release scheduling and progress during execution\nPhase with failed tasks\nStart and stop times for scheduled phases\nEstimated Start and stop times for automatic and manual phases\nEnvironment details\nMaintenance windows\nFreeze Periods\nFailures",
          "page_text": "Release Calendar\nTechDocs\nLogin\n|\nRegister\nContinuous Delivery Director SaaS\nCHANGE VERSION\n1.0\nEnglish\nOverview\nRelease Notes\nAbout Continuous Delivery Director\nGetting Started (SaaS)\nRelease Orchestration\nRelease Design\nRelease Management\nRelease Execution\nRelease Tracks\nCalendars\nRelease Calendar\nMaintenance Windows\nEnvironment Planner\nFreeze Periods\nReports\nTest Orchestration\nSecurity\nIntegrations\nDocumentation Legal Notice\nAdministration\nProduct Tutorial Videos\nReference\nDocumentation Legal Notice\nHome\nContinuous Delivery Director SaaS\n...\nRelease Orchestration\nCalendars\nRelease Calendar\nRelease Calendar\nThe Release Calendar provides a high-level, interactive calendar view of all planned and running releases.\nDownload PDF\nRelease Calendar\nThe Release Calendar provides a high-level, interactive calendar view of all planned and running releases.\nThe calendar acts as a real-time release dashboard with configurations saved per user. Use the calendar to plan resource use across teams and releases. You can see the Releases in separate lines on the left of the calendar.\nYou access the\nRelease Calendar\nfrom the\nCalendars\ntab.\nAs a release owner or member, you can use the visual release calendar to monitor the following information:\nReal-time release scheduling and progress during execution\nPhase with failed tasks\nStart and stop times for scheduled phases\nEstimated Start and stop times for automatic and manual phases\nEnvironment details\nMaintenance windows\nFreeze Periods\nFailures\nConflicts\nThe following conflicts are monitored and are displayed as a red indicator on the left of the phase:\nPhases are scheduled to exceed maintenance windows\nPhases are scheduled to run during a freeze period\nYou can use the following release calendar functionalities to help monitor and manage releases:\nAdd Releases – Select one or more releases to include in the calendar view..\nSelect the +/- icons to the left of the release name to expand the release and show the phases, freeze periods and maintenance windows.\nSelect phases for details.\nDrag and stretch phases in the release to change the schedule duration and execution times. It is recommended to change the “View by” from “Fit Screen” to a specific time frame.\nSelect View by <Duration> and select a time frame from the drop-down list to filter the view.\nSelect a phase to open the\nEdit Phase\nwindow and edit phase details.\nThe release calendar displays the disabled phase only if there are past executions.\nIf there are no executions then the disabled phase is not shown.\nCalendars\nPREVIOUS\nCalendars\nNEXT\nMaintenance Windows\nWas this page helpful?\nDocumentation Feedback\nLast Updated October 26, 2026\nFeedback and Comments\nFirst Name\nLast Name\nEmail\nI have questions/feedback about\nChoose an option...\nBroken hyperlink or page not found\nIncorrect or Missing Content\nOther/General Feedback\nSlow Web Performance\nWhere to find something\nFor comments about a specific page, enter URL\nComments\nI understand and agree to the\nBroadcom\n                      Terms of Use\nand\nPrivacy\n                      Statement\n.\nSecurity Check\n↻\nIncorrect\n                    security answer.\nSubmit Feedback\nThank You!\nThank you for your interest in Broadcom. Your submission has been received.\nClose\nSubmit Feedback\nOther Product Support Resources\nSupport\nSupport Portal\nProduct Communities\nKnowledge Base\nLearning\nBrocade Education\nMainframe Software Education\nSoftware Education\nVMware Learning\nNeed more help?\nVirtual Agent\nAdvanced Support\nContact Us\nWas this page helpful?\nDocumentation Feedback\nLast Updated October 26, 2026\nFeedback and Comments\nFirst Name\nLast Name\nEmail\nI have questions/feedback about\nChoose an option...\nBroken hyperlink or page not found\nIncorrect or Missing Content\nOther/General Feedback\nSlow Web Performance\nWhere to find something\nFor comments about a sp